# This is a byte-exact reconstruction project. Git must not rewrite anything.
#
# The sources are 1990s DOS files staged into a DOSBox build, and the release
# in v1.39b/ is someone else's shipped archive. In both cases the bytes on disk
# ARE the artefact, so line-ending and encoding conversion is disabled outright
# rather than negotiated. `-text` means: never convert on checkin or checkout.

# --- everything, by default: leave the bytes alone ------------------------
* -text

# --- but let git diff the ones worth diffing ------------------------------
# `diff` without `text` gives readable diffs while still never converting EOLs.
*.md    -text diff
*.py    -text diff
*.PAS   -text diff
*.ASM   -text diff
*.INC   -text diff
*.pas   -text diff
*.asm   -text diff
*.inc   -text diff
*.TXT   -text diff
*.CFG   -text diff
*.BAT   -text diff
*.conf  -text diff

# --- genuinely binary: never try -----------------------------------------
*.EXE   binary
*.TPU   binary
*.OBJ   binary
*.TP    binary
*.VTO   binary
*.bin   binary
